@challenge ch-fizzbuzz | FizzBuzz | Easy | false
Print numbers 1 to 30. For multiples of 3 print "Fizz", of 5 "Buzz", of both "FizzBuzz".
:::solution
```dart
void main() {
  for (var i = 1; i <= 30; i++) {
    print(switch ((i % 3, i % 5)) {
      (0, 0) => 'FizzBuzz',
      (0, _) => 'Fizz',
      (_, 0) => 'Buzz',
      _ => '$i',
    });
  }
}
```
:::
@challenge ch-palindrome | Palindrome checker | Easy | false
Write `bool isPalindrome(String s)` that ignores case, spaces and punctuation.
:::solution
```dart
bool isPalindrome(String s) {
  final clean = s.toLowerCase().replaceAll(RegExp(r'[^a-z0-9]'), '');
  return clean == clean.split('').reversed.join();
}
void main() => print(isPalindrome('A man, a plan, a canal: Panama'));
```
:::
@challenge ch-wordcount | Word frequency | Medium | false
Count how often each word appears in a sentence and print the three most common.
:::solution
```dart
void main() {
  const text = 'the cat and the hat and the bat';
  final counts = <String, int>{};
  for (final w in text.split(' ')) {
    counts[w] = (counts[w] ?? 0) + 1;
  }
  final top = counts.entries.toList()..sort((a, b) => b.value.compareTo(a.value));
  print(top.take(3).map((e) => '${e.key}: ${e.value}').join(', '));
}
```
:::
@challenge ch-debounce | Debounced search | Medium | false
Implement a `Debouncer` class that runs an action only after 300 ms without new calls.
:::solution
```dart
import 'dart:async';
class Debouncer {
  Timer? _t;
  void run(void Function() action) {
    _t?.cancel();
    _t = Timer(const Duration(milliseconds: 300), action);
  }
}
void main() {
  final d = Debouncer();
  for (final q in ['f', 'fl', 'flu']) {
    d.run(() => print('search $q'));
  }
}
```
:::
@challenge ch-result | Result type with sealed classes | Hard | true
Create a sealed `Result<T>` with `Ok` and `Err` and a `parsePercent(String)` that returns Err for invalid or out-of-range input.
:::solution
```dart
sealed class Result<T> {}
class Ok<T> extends Result<T> { Ok(this.value); final T value; }
class Err<T> extends Result<T> { Err(this.message); final String message; }
Result<int> parsePercent(String s) {
  final n = int.tryParse(s);
  if (n == null) return Err('Not a number');
  if (n < 0 || n > 100) return Err('Out of range');
  return Ok(n);
}
void main() {
  for (final s in ['42', '120', 'x']) {
    print(switch (parsePercent(s)) { Ok(:final value) => 'ok $value', Err(:final message) => 'error $message' });
  }
}
```
:::
@challenge ch-lru | LRU cache | Hard | true
Implement a generic LRU cache with a fixed capacity using a LinkedHashMap.
:::solution
```dart
class Lru<K, V> {
  Lru(this.capacity);
  final int capacity;
  final _m = <K, V>{};
  V? get(K k) { final v = _m.remove(k); if (v != null) _m[k] = v; return v; }
  void put(K k, V v) { _m.remove(k); _m[k] = v; if (_m.length > capacity) _m.remove(_m.keys.first); }
}
void main() { final c = Lru<String, int>(2)..put('a', 1)..put('b', 2)..get('a')..put('c', 3); print(c.get('b')); }
```
:::
